From 5836033c4e464a0e32d6204fd1961fe96be24df2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:06:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FIX: Force 32 byte alignment of Vec3da independent of AVX2

* MBDblTriIntersectFunc views the ray hit buffer passed by Embree as an
  MBRayHit while the DblTriIntersectFunc it calls views the same buffer as an
  RTCDRayHit. The two struct types only place their 'hit' member at the same
  offset when Vec3da is 32 byte aligned: the extra MBRay members (orientation
  and rh) then fit in the tail padding of RTCDRay. With AVX2 the __m256 union
  member provides that alignment implicitly, but without AVX2 (e.g. on
  aarch64 / arm64 or an x86-64 baseline build) Vec3da is only 8 byte aligned,
  the hit offsets differ by 16 bytes, MBDblTriIntersectFunc never sees the
  hit recorded by DblTriIntersectFunc and restores the original ray, so every
  ray_fire reports no intersection.
* Make the 32 byte alignment explicit so the layout is the same for all
  targets. This is a no-op for AVX2 builds.
---
 include/double_down/Vec3da.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/double_down/Vec3da.h b/include/double_down/Vec3da.h
index e264d74..1148373 100644
--- a/include/double_down/Vec3da.h
+++ b/include/double_down/Vec3da.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 
 namespace double_down {
 
-struct Vec3da {
+struct alignas(32) Vec3da {
   typedef double Scalar;
   enum { n = 3 };
   union{
-- 
